# Handler Version Safety

## The Invariant

Upgrading CAREN MUST be a no-op for existing Clusters. Any change to what a released
handler returns causes Machine rollouts across all managed clusters that use it. This
MUST be prevented. Clusters opt in to new behavior only by naming a new handler version
in their ClusterClass.

## Where Changes Go

All topology mutation handlers, their mutators, and variable discovery handlers live under
`pkg/handlers/vN/`. The highest version is open until a release contains it; every other
version is frozen. `hack/handlers/open-version.sh` prints the open version, or fails if
there is none.

Before modifying anything under `pkg/handlers/vN/` or `api/v1alpha1/`, ask:

1. Does this change what `GeneratePatches` returns for any input? (New, removed or
   changed patches, or a new mutator enabled by default.)
2. Does this change what `DiscoverVariables` returns? (Schemas and defaults; defaults
   change the variables passed to `GeneratePatches`.)

If yes to either:

1. Change only the open version. If there is none, run `make handlers.new-version` first.
2. Run `make go-generate` after API changes; it copies the CRDs into the latest version only.
3. Run `make handlers.golden-update` and check that the golden diff contains only the
   intended change, and only for the open version.

Never modify a released `pkg/handlers/vN/`, its golden files, corpus inputs, or remove a
released handler name to make a change fit. `make handlers.check-frozen` fails on all of
these. The `frozen-handler-override` label only allows a fix to released handler code that
leaves its golden output unchanged.

## When a New Version Is NOT Required

- Any change to the open version, with its golden files regenerated.
- Changes to lifecycle handlers (`pkg/handlers/lifecycle/`) and webhooks, which are not
  versioned.

## Verification

- `make test` runs the golden tests in `pkg/handlers/golden/`.
- `make handlers.check-frozen` compares against the last release.
- `make e2e-test E2E_LABEL='provider:Docker' E2E_FOCUS='Upgrade'` upgrades CAREN under a
  Cluster created from the last release and fails on any topology change or rollout.

See `docs/content/contributing/handler_versions.md`.
